.Dd June 17, 2026
.Dt LOG-ROTATE 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm log-rotate
.Nd rotate launchd service logs with compression
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar service-name
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
rotates a service's log file by gzip-compressing the current content into a
timestamped archive and truncating the active log. The truncation is in place,
so a service holding the file descriptor open keeps writing without a
restart \(em safe for live daemons.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -dry-run
Show what would happen without rotating.
.It Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1
.It 0
Rotation succeeded
.Pq or dry-run preview printed .
.It 1
Error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li log-rotate otel-collector
Compress and truncate the OTel Collector log.
.It Li log-rotate openobserve --dry-run
Preview the rotation without changing anything.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openobserve-ctl 8 ,
.Xr zsvc 8
